# Workstream coordination

- Four lanes exist: Integration/Coordinator, TradeStation/Broker,
  Gmail/Signal Ingestion, and Database/PostgreSQL Infrastructure.
- Only Lane 1 may propose integrating certified specialist work into
  canonical `main`. Specialists may not self-certify and self-integrate.
- Read `docs/WORKSTREAM_STATUS.md`, `docs/WORKSTREAM_OWNERSHIP.md`,
  `docs/WORKSTREAM_DEPENDENCIES.md`, and `docs/INTEGRATION_PROTOCOL.md`
  before cross-lane or integration work.
- Resolve conflicts by the Level 0–6 hierarchy in
  `docs/WORKSTREAM_OWNERSHIP.md`. Conversations never override accepted
  contracts or canonical main.
- Preserve existing specialist PR histories (including draft PR #21 and
  PR #22). Do not recreate those branches only to rename them. Do not
  auto-merge or reconstruct stale PR #19.
- Concurrent writers require separate worktrees or isolated checkouts.
  No force pushes, no automatic post-certification rebases, and no
  cross-lane cherry-picks without Lane 1 authorization.
- Overlapping edits to coordination-sensitive files require explicit
  reconciliation. If incompatible contracts collide, return
  `CROSS_WORKSTREAM_CONTRACT_CONFLICT` and stop silent selection.
- Proposed ADRs are not Accepted. Passing tests are not integration
  approval. Provider confirmation is not operational certification.
- Dependency IDs in `docs/WORKSTREAM_DEPENDENCIES.md` are stable. Do not
  mark another lane's dependency resolved without evidence.
- This bootstrap and coordination layer authorize no TradeStation auth,
  Gmail auth, Supabase connection, paid database, remote migration,
  credential provisioning, or `LIVE` path.
